REGENT OF BANYUWANGI

REGENT OF BANYUWANGI

REGIONAL REGULATION OF BANYUWANGI REGENCY

NUMBER 1 OF 2011

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE AND HUMAN TRAFFICKING

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF BANYUWANGI,

Considering : a. that violence against women and children as well as human trafficking constitutes an act of degrading human dignity and degree so that they need to be provided with adequate services and protection;

b. that the level of human trafficking, violence against women and children is still high, therefore it is the obligation of the regional government to regulate and serve the interests of the community in this case women and children victims of violence and human trafficking;

c. that in order for the handling of human trafficking, violence against women and children to be implemented effectively and efficiently, it is necessary to regulate the protection of women and children victims of violence and human trafficking;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a, b and c, it is necessary to establish a regional regulation on the Protection of Women and

Children Victims of Violence and Human Trafficking.

