Article 21

The Regent in implementing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children who are victims of violence and human trafficking, makes efforts to:

a. coordinate the implementation of policies, programs, and activities among SKPD;
b. cooperate with other regencies and cities within one province, and with regencies and cities in other provinces, in the implementation of policies, programs and activities in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
c. facilitate and provide services;
d. implement affirmative action for the protection of women and children and human trafficking; and
e. develop a data system for the protection of women and children, including a data system on violence against women and children and human trafficking.
